### Subcommands with Struct Variants in Rust Clap Derive

Source: https://docs.rs/clap/latest/src/clap/_derive/_tutorial.rs.html?search=

Illustrates how to define subcommands using struct variants with `#[derive(Subcommand)]`. This approach is useful for creating distinct commands within a single CLI application, each with its own set of arguments and behavior.

```rust
use clap::{Parser, Subcommand};

#[derive(Parser)]
struct Cli {
    #[command(subcommand)]
    command: Commands,
}

#[derive(Subcommand)]
enum Commands {
    /// Adds files to myproject
    Add,
    /// Removes files from myproject
    Remove,
}

fn main() {
    let cli = Cli::parse();

    match &cli.command {
        Commands::Add => {
            println!("Executing add command");
        }
        Commands::Remove => {
            println!("Executing remove command");
        }
    }
}
```

