### Flattening Custom Args into Derived Structs

Source: https://docs.rs/clap/latest/src/clap/_derive/mod.rs.html?search=u32+-%3E+bool

Explains how to use the #[command(flatten)] attribute with a struct that manually implements the Args trait to inject arguments into a derived CLI struct.

```rust
use clap::{Args, Parser};

struct MyCustomArgs {
    verbose: bool,
}

impl Args for MyCustomArgs {
    fn augment_args(cmd: clap::Command) -> clap::Command {
        cmd.arg(clap::Arg::new("verbose").long("verbose"))
    }
    fn augment_args_for_update(cmd: clap::Command) -> clap::Command {
        cmd
    }
}

#[derive(Parser)]
struct Cli {
    #[command(flatten)]
    extra: MyCustomArgs,
}
```

